  "question": {
    "text": "The figure shows a block of mass m resting on a horizontal smooth floor at a distance <math><mi>l</mi></math> from a rigid wall. Block is pushed toward the right by a distance <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> and released from rest. When block passes from its mean position, another block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is gently placed on it which sticks to it due to friction. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> so that the combined block just touches the left wall is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi></math>. Find the value of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">η</mi></math>.<br />\r<br />\r<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/4e3c6699-d22f-409c-822c-3259e1a329a4-image17.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"height: 116px; width: 250px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "When block P is released from rest from a distance <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> toward right from mean position, this will be the amplitude of oscillation so velocity of block when passing from its mean position is given as<br /><math><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math><br />If mass m<sub>1</sub> is added to it and just after if velocity of combined block becomes v<sub>1</sub>, from momentum conservation, we have<br />mv = (m + m<sub>1</sub>)v<sub>1</sub><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math><br />If this is the velocity of combined block at mean position, it is given as<br /><math><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> where <math><msub><mrow><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math><br />where A<sub>1</sub> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> are the new amplitude and angular frequency of SHM of the block.<br />It is given that combined block just reaches the left wall.<br />Thus, the new amplitude of oscillation must be <math><mi>l</mi></math> . So, we have,<br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mi>l</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math><br />On solving, we get<br /><math><msub><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>m</mi></math><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>",
    "image": null
  },
